			<div class="content-sections">
				<div class="timeline-sections">
				<span class="timeline-spine" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="timeline-spine__fill"></span>
					<span class="timeline-spine__origin"></span>
				</span>
				<section id="experience" class="content-section experience-section" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
					<header class="content-heading"><h2 id="experience-title">Work experience</h2></header>
					<div class="experience-timeline">
						<article class="experience-entry">
							<p class="entry-meta">Sezakompjuteri · 2022 - Present</p>
							<h3>Lead Software Engineer - Owner</h3>
							<p>Lead engineer responsible for the technical vision, architecture, and long-term development of Sezakompjuteri, a computer hardware marketplace platform. Led every stage of the software lifecycle, from initial planning and technology selection to deployment, infrastructure, and ongoing maintenance.</p>
							<ul class="responsibility-list">
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Selected the technology stack, frameworks, development tools, and architectural patterns to ensure scalability, maintainability, and long-term growth.</span></li>
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Designed and implemented the entire application from the ground up, including backend services, frontend, database, authentication, security, and supporting systems.</span></li>
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Directed feature planning, performance optimization, system scalability, and overall product scope throughout the project's lifecycle.</span></li>
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Owned deployment, hosting, CI/CD automation, server administration, and operational maintenance to ensure reliable production releases.</span></li>
							</ul>

							<div class="skill-group skill-group--languages">
								<dd><ul class="skill-pills"><li>C#</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Python</li><li>ASP.NET Core</li><li>Angular</li><li>Entity Framework Core</li><li>MSSQL</li><li>Git</li></ul></dd>
							</div>
						</article>

						<article class="experience-entry">
							<p class="entry-meta">DalMax Frigo · 2025 - Present</p>
							<h3>Lead Software Engineer - Contract</h3>
							<p>Collaborating directly with company leadership to redesign and modernize the organization's online presence through an interactive, high-performance website that showcases construction projects using real-time 3D visualization.</p>
							<ul class="responsibility-list">
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Designing and developing a modern landing page with interactive 3D experiences to better showcase the company's services and completed projects.</span></li>
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Implementing a Three.js-based 3D viewer capable of visualizing construction projects through segmented build phases and interactive scene controls.</span></li>
							    <li><span class="responsibility-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Optimizing rendering performance and responsiveness to ensure a smooth experience across desktop and mobile devices.</span></li>
							</ul>
							<div class="skill-group skill-group--languages">
								<dd><ul class="skill-pills"><li>Html</li><li>CSS</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>Express.js</li><li>Three.js</li></ul></dd>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</section>
				<section id="projects" class="content-section projects-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
					<header class="content-heading"><h2 id="projects-title">Projects in Active <br> Development</h2></header>
					<div class="project-timeline">
						<article class="project-template project-template--private">
							<div>
								<div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project status">
									<span class="project-meta__category">Full End-to-End OCR Pipeline for Desktop</span>
									<span class="project-meta__status">Active development</span>
									<span class="project-meta__release">No public release yet</span>
								</div>
								<h3>GlujLens</h3>
								<p>GlujLens is a high-performance Multi-Platform OCR platform built around a custom multi-model AI pipeline. By combining lightweight vision models with configurable OCR and translation providers, it delivers accurate text detection, recognition, and translation while utilizing CPU, GPU, or NPU acceleration through ROCm, CUDA, and Vulkan for efficient inference across a wide range of hardware.</p>
							</div>
							<ul class="project-tags"> 
								<li>C#</li>
								<li>Python</li>  
								<li>.NET 9</li>
							    <li>Avalonia UI</li>
							    <li>U-Net</li>
							    <li>PyTorch</li>
							    <li>CUDA</li>
							    <li>ROCm</li>
							    <li>Vulkan</li>
								<li>Multi-Platform</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="project-access-state">
								<span class="project-access-state__icon" aria-hidden="true">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3M12 14v2"/></svg>
								</span>
								<span><strong>Proprietary project</strong><small>Source code, models, and development builds are private.</small></span>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article class="project-template project-template--public">
							<div>
								<div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project status">
									<span class="project-meta__category">Vendor-neutral hardware benchmark for Windows</span>
									<span class="project-meta__version">Beta · Version 0.1.0</span>
									<span class="project-meta__release project-meta__release--public">Public release</span>
								</div>
								<h3>Gluj-Bench</h3>
								<p>Gluj-Bench is a free, vendor-neutral hardware benchmarking suite built in Rust to evaluate modern desktop systems. It measures CPU and GPU compute performance alongside cache, RAM, VRAM, and host-to-GPU bandwidth using transparent, reproducible workloads.</p>
							</div>
							<ul class="project-tags"><li>Rust</li><li>eframe/egui</li><li>wgpu</li><li>WGSL</li><li>Windows x64</li><li>MIT</li></ul>
							<div class="project-actions" aria-label="Gluj-Bench links">
								<a class="project-action project-action--source" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Gluj-Bench" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h13a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3"/></svg>
									<span>View source</span>
								</a>
								<a class="project-action project-action--release" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Gluj-Bench/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0 4-4m-4 4-4-4M4 19h16"/></svg>
									<span>Get releases</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article class="project-template project-template--public project-template--drive">
							<div>
								<div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project status">
									<span class="project-meta__category">Windows-native private media server</span>
									<span class="project-meta__version">Beta · Version 0.1.0</span>
									<span class="project-meta__release project-meta__release--public">Public release</span>
								</div>
								<h3>Gluj-Drive</h3>
								<p>Gluj-Drive turns a Windows PC into a private photo and video library for LAN or Tailscale access. It indexes media in existing folders without reorganizing the originals, provides responsive desktop and mobile galleries, streams video, supports uploads, and offers optional fully local semantic search.</p>
							</div>
							<ul class="project-tags"><li>C#</li><li>ASP.NET Core</li><li>React</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>TinyCLIP</li><li>Windows x64</li><li>Apache 2.0</li></ul>
							<div class="project-actions" aria-label="Gluj-Drive links">
								<a class="project-action project-action--source" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Gluj-Drive" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h13a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3"/></svg>
									<span>View source</span>
								</a>
								<a class="project-action project-action--release" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Gluj-Drive/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0 4-4m-4 4-4-4M4 19h16"/></svg>
									<span>Get releases</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</article>
