					<section class="project-archive" aria-labelledby="project-archive-title">
						<header class="project-archive__heading">
							<span class="project-archive__terminal" aria-hidden="true"></span>
							<p>Archive / resolved threads</p>
							<h3 id="project-archive-title">Past project matrix</h3>
							<p>Finished work, paused explorations, and projects retired along the way.</p>
						</header>
						<div class="project-archive__grid">
							<article class="archive-project archive-project--finished">
								<div class="archive-project__meta"><span class="archive-project__status">Finished</span><span>Vision-Capable AI Assistant</span></div>
								<h4>AI-Backseater</h4>
								<p>A Windows desktop companion that captures a selected screen region and sends it, together with a custom persona and instruction prompt, to an OpenAI-compatible vision endpoint. Depending on the prompt, it can provide gaming commentary, video analysis, or guided instruction.</p>
								<p class="archive-project__outcome">The finished application combines local Kokoro text-to-speech, rolling conversation context, alert conditions, and searchable SQLite history in one configurable assistant. Hardware requirements depend on the selected vision model, with larger local models requiring significantly more VRAM.</p>
								<ul class="archive-project__tags"><li>Python</li><li>PyQt5</li><li>Vision LLM</li><li>OpenAI API</li><li>Kokoro TTS</li><li>SQLite</li></ul>
								<a class="archive-project__link" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/AI-Backseater" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
							</article>
							<article class="archive-project archive-project--paused">
								<div class="archive-project__meta"><span class="archive-project__status">Paused</span><span>Interactive Map Generator</span></div>
								<h4>GujGen</h4>
								<p>An experimental desktop toolkit for generating and editing fantasy worlds. It combines seeded, grid-based terrain generation with visual markers for shaping landmasses, biomes, mountain ranges, rivers, and other world features.</p>
								<p class="archive-project__outcome">Development was paused as the project’s scope and architectural complexity grew, while primary development focus shifted to GlujLens.</p>
								<ul class="archive-project__tags"><li>C#</li><li>.NET 9</li><li>Avalonia</li><li>MVVM</li><li>Perlin Noise</li><li>JSON</li></ul>
								<a class="archive-project__link" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/GujGen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
							</article>
							<article class="archive-project archive-project--cancelled">
								<div class="archive-project__meta"><span class="archive-project__status">Cancelled</span><span>Hardware Price Aggregator</span></div>
								<h4>BitCeni</h4>
								<p>A full-stack hardware price aggregation prototype built around a Django REST API, an Angular frontend, and a Selenium scraper. It was intended to normalize listings from multiple retailers so users could compare the best available purchasing options.</p>
								<p class="archive-project__outcome">Frequent retailer-page changes required continuous scraper maintenance and made reliable price aggregation too unreliable to continue.</p>
								<ul class="archive-project__tags"><li>Python</li><li>Django REST</li><li>Angular</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Selenium</li></ul>
								<a class="archive-project__link" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/BitCeni" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
							</article>
							<article class="archive-project archive-project--finished">
								<div class="archive-project__meta"><span class="archive-project__status">Finished</span><span>Proof of Concept</span></div>
								<h4>Service-Status-Dashboard</h4>
								<p>A compact service-monitoring dashboard built with Node.js and Express. It tracks HTTP service availability and response times through a REST API, an EJS web interface, and SQLite persistence through Sequelize.</p>
								<p class="archive-project__outcome">The completed proof of concept demonstrates a full CI/CD workflow: GitHub Actions runs unit and integration tests, verifies the application inside Docker, builds a production image, and publishes it to Docker Hub.</p>
								<ul class="archive-project__tags"><li>Node.js</li><li>Express</li><li>SQLite</li><li>Sequelize</li><li>Docker</li><li>GitHub Actions</li><li>Jest</li></ul>
								<a class="archive-project__link" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Service-Status-Dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
							</article>
							<article class="archive-project archive-project--paused">
								<div class="archive-project__meta"><span class="archive-project__status">Paused</span><span>Roguelike Game</span></div>
								<h4>Cave-Game</h4>
								<p>My role was to design a scalable, data-driven foundation that made content creation and ongoing development easier for the team, using Godot and C# as the technical base.</p>
								<p class="archive-project__outcome">Development is paused while the team waits for additional game assets.</p>
								<ul class="archive-project__tags"><li>Godot</li><li>C#</li><li>Data-Driven Design</li><li>Game Development</li></ul>
								<p class="archive-project__access"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span> Private repository</p>
							</article>
						</div>
